config OMNISIGHT_RK3588_TYPEC_TCPC
	tristate "OmniSight RK3588 Type-C TCPC binding"
	depends on I2C
	depends on TYPEC
	select TYPEC_TCPM
	select TYPEC_FUSB302
	help
	  Bind the ATK-DLRK3588 Type-C controller to the upstream Linux
	  Type-C controller driver. The default controller is FUSB302, matching
	  the C5.C.0 spike and the RK3588 design assumption.

	  This shim instantiates the upstream I2C client and leaves TCPM
	  registration plus /sys/class/typec exposure to the selected upstream
	  driver. It does not implement UCSI or userspace PD contract policy.

	  HUSB311 and FUSB304 are intentionally not enabled here because the
	  C5.C.0 spike did not find a mainline-compatible driver binding for
	  those alternates. WUSB3801 may be instantiated for attach/orientation
	  smoke only, but it is not equivalent to FUSB302-class TCPM PD.

config OMNISIGHT_TYPEC_UCSI_BINDINGS
	tristate "OmniSight Type-C UCSI bindings"
	depends on TYPEC
	depends on UCSI
	help
	  Register a board-supplied UCSI transport with the upstream Linux UCSI
	  core so connector status, PD contract state, and alternate modes are
	  exposed through /sys/class/typec.

	  This is a narrow binding layer only. It does not instantiate the
	  RK3588 Type-C controller from C5.C.1 and does not implement the
	  charging daemon or userspace PD policy from C5.C.3.
